  - name: "Symbiotic Link to Korallyte"
    description: "The shaper grows Korallyte on itself like a second skin - a thin flexible suit making the naut''yll look like an elemental being of alien metal, worth anywhere from 15 to 150 M.D.C. and typically 40 to 80. Up to 15 M.D.C. worth per level of experience can be linked. For 5 I.S.P. it turns armoured fingers into claws or blades (a pair does 2D4 M.D.), shapes a short sword (2D6 M.D.) or long sword (3D6 M.D.) from a forearm, or covers the body in spikes (1D4 M.D. each). Through psionic union the armour comes alive and lashes out as clawed whips or tentacles for 1D6 M.D. per strike per level, with half the shaper''s combat bonuses and one attack per melee - two at level 10, or three if its master is knocked unconscious. It regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. per minute; if it is destroyed the Korallyte is dead and a new link takes five days of continual meditation."
  - name: "Korallyte Energy Blast"
    description: "By burning off some of the living armour the shaper fires an energy blast doing 1D4 M.D. per M.D.C. point consumed, to a maximum of 15 M.D.C. in one blast."
  - name: "Sense Korallyte"
    description: "Tells by touch or by sight within 50 feet (15.2 m) whether something is made of Korallyte, and has a 30% +5% per level chance of sensing the organisms that create it within two miles (3.2 km)."
  - name: "Gather Korallyte Producing Organisms"
    description: "Psionically communes with and gathers the mollusc that secretes Korallyte. The shaper finds a breeding ground, enters a deep meditative trance, and the molluscs gather around it; they are then moved to a contained underwater area, rather like a fish hatchery. They are extremely valuable and always handled with care."
extraction_notes: |
  - THE NAUT''YLL RACIAL STAT BLOCK IS PRINTED 148 AND IS FOLDED INTO EACH OF
    THE THREE CLASSES rather than shipped as a fourth row. The Experience
    Tables on printed 214 name the Soldier, the Devastator and the Koral
    Shaper separately and give the bare race no ladder; printed 148 is a
    shared preamble - attributes, M.D.C., depth tolerance, water dependency,
    the amphibious abilities - that all three build on. Every one of them
    carries the same racial restrictions and natural abilities, deliberately,
    so a reader of one class never has to go and find the other page.
  - ITS COMBAT BONUSES ARE UNDERWATER-ONLY AND ARE STORED ANYWAY, the same
    exception made for the Amphib and for the same reason: the water is this
    race''s normal condition rather than a temporary state, and a sheet showing
    no bonuses at all would be wrong more often than right.
  - NO PSIONICS BLOCK. Printed 148 rolls the tier and leaves half of all
    naut''yll with nothing, so granting one would give powers to characters who
    have none - the same call made on the dolphin, the orca and the Sea Titan.
  - SPD IS THE LAND SPEED, which for this race is 3D4 - barely a walk. The
    underwater speed of 6D6+10 is in the restrictions.
  - ITS source_book CITES THE CLASS PAGES ONLY, 151-152, not the racial block
    on 148 that it also carries. A first draft wrote "p.148, 151-152" and
    class-check warned that it matched no title or alias - the resolver reads a
    single `p.N-M` range, and a comma-separated one resolves to nothing, which
    would have made every field on this class untraceable. The racial page is
    named in the first note above instead.
  - ITS TWO SIGNATURE SPELLS ARE GRANTED BY NAME and were imported in #799:
    `Shape Koral` and `Koral Blast`, the only two spells in this book stored
    without a tradition prefix. Everything else it starts with is six ocean
    spells from levels one to six.
  - ITS PER-LEVEL SPELL GRANT IS CAPPED AT THE CHARACTER''S OWN LEVEL, the same
    shape as the Ocean Wizard''s - `spells_per_level_levels:
    up_to_character_level`. The creation picks are capped at level six instead,
    which is a different cap and is in the starting group''s note.
  - IT IS A MAJOR PSIONIC WITH A REAL GRANT, unlike every other naut''yll: six
    powers from any category EXCEPT super, and one more per level. That
    exclusion is why `categories_allowed` lists the three lesser categories
    rather than being omitted.
  - THE KORALLYTE ABILITIES ARE ALL PROSE and could not be otherwise. An I.S.P.
    cost per pound of material, a living armour with its own M.D.C., attacks and
    regeneration, and a blast that consumes that armour are four resources the
    app has no shape for. They are `natural_abilities` with the full rules in
    them.
  - ITS RELATED LIST IS THE NARROWEST OF THE THREE NAUT''YLL CLASSES and the only
    one that opens Medical entirely. Transcribed as printed 152 gives it.
