# Naut''Yll Koral Shaper

## Lore

The koral shaper is the oldest and most revered of the naut''yll magic practitioners - a special breed of magician and psionic who developed a unique relationship with the Korallyte, a mollusc that secretes a metal-hard substance of the same name.

The early shamans found that magic and psionics could coax Korallyte formations to grow and reform, and that a shape could be dissolved and remade into something else. A knife becomes a digging tool, an axe, a spoon, a plate. Korallyte armour repairs itself or sprouts claws, spikes and blades. A few pieces of the stuff could give a whole tribe every tool and weapon it needed.

As the naut''yll advanced, the use of Korallyte became more sophisticated and far deadlier: body armour, weapon casings, the hulls of vehicles. A koral shaper controls it to an astonishing degree, manipulating it in hundreds of ways and even turning it into pure energy for an attack.

## GM Notes

Koral shapers are an important part of the naut''yll military. Most stay behind the lines shaping weapons and armour and repairing Korallyte items, but a shaper may be attached to a special forces team, and occasionally an entire warband of them is sent on a mission.

Every magician except a warlock can learn the Korallyte-shaping spells. Only the koral shaper gets the most out of the material.

The molluscs themselves are native only to the naut''yll homeworld and have never been successfully transplanted anywhere else - which quietly limits how much Korallyte exists on Rifts Earth.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nautyll-koral-shaper');


